    "show_share": true,
    "description": "AKU's School of Nursing and Midwifery (SONAM) not only offers academic training for practising nurses and midwives but also provides its faculty opportunities for career development. Following approval of two Master's programmes by Kenya's Commission for University Education, SONAM collaborated with the Liverpool John Moores University (LJMU) on a fellowship programme for four of its faculty. The fellowship began on February 24, 2020, and was to last six weeks but was cut short by the COVID-19 pandemic. The four faculty were Dr Eunice Siaity-Pallangyo, Academic Head, SONAM Tanzania; Dr Rachel Kimani, faculty, SONAM Kenya; Dr Grace Nakate, faculty SONAM Uganda; and Ms Lucy Kisaka, faculty, SONAM  Tanzania.",
